---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title={`${site.title} — Privacy`}
  description="What this site does and does not collect."
>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    This site sets no cookies and has no accounts. It counts visits anonymously.
  </p>

  <h2>What is collected</h2>
  <p>
    This site counts visits with <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare
    Web Analytics</a>. It is cookieless and uses no fingerprinting or cross-site identifiers. For each visit it
    records:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>the page viewed, to see which pages get read;</li>
    <li>the referring site and country, to see where readers come from;</li>
    <li>the device type and browser, to make sure the site displays well on them;</li>
    <li>how long the page took to load, to keep it fast.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Nothing else is recorded, and none of it is personally identifiable. There is no advertising, and
    nothing is sold or shared.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your chosen theme is remembered in your own browser's local storage, never transmitted anywhere,
    and removed when you clear your site data.
  </p>

  <h2>What is hosted elsewhere</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by GitHub Pages, which keeps its own server logs. Book covers on
    the <a href={`${base}/reads`}>Reads</a> page are loaded from Goodreads, so your browser requests them from
    Goodreads directly.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If something here is unclear, or you would like to ask about anything on this
    page, <a href={site.links.find((l) => l.label === 'Email')?.href} rel="noopener">get in touch</a>.
  </p>

  <style>
    ul {
      padding-inline-start: 1.1rem;
    }

    li {
      margin-block: 0.4rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
